{"id":"soft-countriana","title":"Soft Countriana","url":"https://aesthetics.fandom.com/wiki/Soft_Countriana","rev":240290,"fetched":"2026-10-16","lead":[{"t":"p","c":[{"t":"b","c":["Soft Countriana"]}," is a ",{"t":"a","c":["country"],"href":"https://aesthetics.fandom.com/wiki/Country"},"-inspired aesthetic that was popular in media in the late 1970s to 1980s and was popularized by conservative suburban communities, as a way of holding onto tradition and history. It can also be seen as an early form of ",{"t":"a","c":["Cottagecore"],"href":"https://aesthetics.fandom.com/wiki/Cottagecore"},"."]}],"sections":[{"title":"History","id":"history","blocks":[{"t":"p","c":["This aesthetic likely came out of the rise of right wing beliefs in the 1980s, suburbanization, and the influence of ",{"t":"a","c":["Victorian"],"href":"https://aesthetics.fandom.com/wiki/Victorian"}," and ",{"t":"a","c":["Gay Nineties revival"],"id":"gay-nineties-revival"}," aesthetics. Victorian architecture was popular at this time."]}]},{"title":"Philosophy","id":"philosophy","blocks":[{"t":"p","c":["Similar to Cottagecore, this aesthetic insinuates the feeling of wanting to get away from modern society, but with more of a reminiscent, suburbanized feel compared to the colonial one of Cottagecore."]}]},{"title":"Fashion","id":"fashion","blocks":[{"t":"p","c":["Though this would be more of an aesthetic prevalent in interior design, the fashion is quite feminine, including:"]},{"t":"ul","items":[{"c":["Gunne Sax-style dresses"]},{"c":["Laura Ashley fashions"]},{"c":["Frilly nightwear (more specifically nightgowns)"]},{"c":["Quilt skirts"]},{"c":["Ruffled tops"]},{"c":["Polka dot dresses"]},{"c":["Peter Pan collars"]},{"c":["Puffed sleeves"]}]}]},{"title":"Visuals","id":"visuals","blocks":[{"t":"ul","items":[{"c":["Frilly nightwear"]},{"c":["Quilts"]},{"c":["Checkered or polka dot patterns"]},{"c":[{"t":"a","c":["Shabby Chic"],"id":"shabby-chic"}," knick-knacks"]},{"c":["Jars, presumably for salt, sugar, etc."]},{"c":["Rocking horses, teddy bears, dollhouses and other children’s paraphernalia"]},{"c":["Geese, particularly in the likes of Mother Goose for the vintage feel"]}]}]},{"title":"Media","id":"media","blocks":[{"t":"h","l":3,"c":["Brands"]},{"t":"ul","items":[{"c":["Hello Kitty"]},{"c":["Barbie"]},{"c":["Precious Moments"]},{"c":["Cabbage Patch Kids"]},{"c":["Auntie 'Em Collection"]},{"c":["Peter Rabbit"]},{"c":["Country home magazines"]}]}]},{"title":"Gallery","id":"gallery","blocks":[{"t":"gallery","items":[{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/b/b5/3FD7A46F-F68F-444A-8623-AF00B9E9EDEE.jpeg/revision/latest?cb=20230418070124","w":185,"h":185,"cap":["An example of a Countriana kitchen"]},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/b/b2/713E9D20-FD26-454D-8D05-4E1CA2E38BD6.png/revision/latest?cb=20230314224300","w":185,"h":185,"cap":["A vintage bedroom from the 1980s"]},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/5/53/BBBF3183-56D9-4545-9FE1-86C3C5CCDFB8.jpeg/revision/latest?cb=20230418065632","w":185,"h":185,"cap":["A country living room"]},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/f/fe/9D958DDC-B7DB-4757-8756-93C1A6FF2F1E.webp/revision/latest?cb=20230418081759","w":185,"h":185,"cap":["A party table adorned in pastels"]},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/b/b4/771A7C11-2965-4315-AED8-7C2B6A3A0687.webp/revision/latest?cb=20230418081834","w":185,"h":185,"cap":["Example of Soft Countriana fashion"]},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/6/63/B3A7CF92-FC6A-44EC-9422-29BE86946685.webp/revision/latest?cb=20230418081855","w":185,"h":185,"cap":["Baby room"]},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/8/8d/1033C4D8-F9E2-4F00-8024-C61DE86290D9.webp/revision/latest?cb=20230420033956","w":185,"h":185,"cap":["Soft Countriana lamp"]},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/a/a2/C291AF33-2F19-498B-B5BC-67DA58A4E4A9.web